            <div xml:id="d270">

                <pb facs="0317" n="1151" xml:id="pg1151"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 657.119/364a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-15T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 15, 1918—5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6905. For Sheldon [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 212. Please repeat the following to Schmedeman: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p> Nansen states that his Government is aware of the fact that you have
                            copy of proposed draft of Norwegian agreement. He asks that this draft
                            be submitted to his Government, and we have not felt that we could
                            refuse without exciting suspicion on part of Norwegian Government,
                            although we would have preferred to have first gone over the draft with
                            Nansen here. You are accordingly authorized to acquaint the Norwegian
                            Government with the terms of draft which Sheldon furnished you, at the
                            same time emphasizing that this draft is preliminary and tentative only
                            and that it will now be made the subject of discussion with Doctor
                            Nansen.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
